---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import site from '../data/site.json';
import { allQuestions, allPapers, FIRST_SERIES } from '../lib/data';
---
<Base title="About this site" context="about" description="Who runs lawaleveltutor.com and where the questions, mark schemes and ratings come from.">
  <h1>About this site</h1>
  <p>lawaleveltutor.com is run by {site.company}, an A-level tutoring business with a small team of specialist tutors. The site exists to give OCR Law students the past-paper material they actually use, sorted the way they revise, free and without sign-up; and to introduce students who want more help to a tutor who teaches the OCR specification.</p>
  <h2>Where the material comes from</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Questions, mark schemes and examiner comments</strong> are from OCR's own published papers for every Law series since {FIRST_SERIES} (H418 A level and H018 AS), with OCR's sample assessment papers: {allPapers.length} papers and {allQuestions.length} questions. Each question has been tagged to the specification content it assesses, its assessment objectives and its question type. The nature of law essays that OCR prints on both Paper 3 and Paper 4 are counted once.</li>
    <li><strong>Difficulty ratings</strong> (easy, medium, hard) are our reading of what the examiners' report says about how candidates found each question. OCR's Law reports do not print average marks, so treat the ratings as a guide. Sample papers have no report and are rated by comparison.</li>
    <li><strong>Topic tags</strong> were made by the site and are being checked by our tutor; tell us if one looks wrong.</li>
    <li><strong>Key-term cards</strong> are original, written for this site; nothing derived from OCR's material is generated automatically.</li>
    <li><strong>Grade boundaries and exam dates</strong> are OCR's published figures; the pages say where each was taken from.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Who writes it</h2>
  <p>The tutoring is by Sue, our A-level Law tutor; see the <a href="/tutors/">tutor page</a>. The site is built and maintained by the same small team that runs <a href="https://www.alevelbiologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelbiologytutor.com</a>, <a href="https://www.mathsaleveltutor.com" rel="noopener">mathsaleveltutor.com</a>, <a href="https://www.alevelpsychologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelpsychologytutor.com</a>, <a href="https://www.alevelsociologytutor.com" rel="noopener">alevelsociologytutor.com</a> and <a href="https://www.economicsaleveltutor.com" rel="noopener">economicsaleveltutor.com</a>.</p>
  <h2>Mistakes</h2>
  <p>If you find one, tell us on the <a href="/report/">report a mistake</a> page; corrections usually go live the same week.</p>
</Base>
